WEBVTT

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.096
I've always thought about burnout
as emotional exhaustion,

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.006
but exhaustion that's persistent

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.526
and also seriously impairs
your functioning.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.217
AHP: Yeah.

00:05:38.241 --> 00:05:41.772
AG: And what you're describing
sounds more like just plain stress.

00:05:41.796 --> 00:05:43.734
AHP: I think it's very similar to stress

00:05:43.758 --> 00:05:47.536
and there's a fine line
between having a lot of anxiety

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:51.046
and being depressed,
and what we consider burnout.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:54.766
I think that it's all
of those things at once.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.773
You know the emotional component to it,
I think, is very real.

00:05:57.797 --> 00:05:59.161
But I think it impairs you,

00:05:59.185 --> 00:06:01.978
but not so much
that you entirely collapse, right?